{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [2, 3, 6, 6] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, here's one way to do it:", "start": 0, "end": 113, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(6 / (3 - 2)) × 6 = 24", "start": 115, "end": 137, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's break it down:", "start": 139, "end": 159, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1. First, calculate the expression inside the parentheses: 3 - 2 = 1.", "start": 161, "end": 230, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "2. Then, divide 6 by 1: 6 / 1 = 6.", "start": 231, "end": 265, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "3. Finally, multiply the result by 6: 6 × 6 = 24.", "start": 266, "end": 315, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Thus, the expression (6 / (3 - 2)) × 6 equals 24.", "start": 317, "end": 366, "label": "inform"}
